title: VMware Aria Automation: Service instance on a node
agents: aria_automation
catalog: app/vmware
license: GPLv2
distribution: kuhn-ruess
description:
 Monitors the instance of an Aria Automation service (pod) on the queried
 node, taken from '/api/v1/services/cluster'.

 The state is {OK} if the instance is "running", {CRIT} otherwise. The health
 "healthy" is {OK}, "degraded" and "warning" are {WARN}, "unknown" is {UNKN},
 every other value is {CRIT}. The health message is shown if set.

 If the service still exists in the cluster but has no instance on this node
 any more (a single instance service moved to another node), the service goes
 {WARN} and names the nodes it runs on. The state is set in the rule
 "VMware Aria Automation node service".

 CPU, memory and disk usage as reported by Aria are shown and stored as
 metrics.

item:
 The name of the Aria Automation service, for example "rabbitmq-ha".

discovery:
 One service per service instance running on the node.
